      "content": "That's definitely getting closer to the vibe I want. \n\nI noticed a real difference in how you're describing the \"quality\" of the surroundings. For the first property, the language is very stable and high-status—words like 'distinguished' and 'unblemished.' For the second one, it's more about 'energy' and 'new waves.'\n\nJust to help me fine-tune the marketing strategy, can you explain why you chose those specific linguistic directions for each? Like, why does a 'legacy' property need a different vocabulary than a property in a 'dynamic' urban area? I want to make sure I'm being intentional with how we differentiate the prestige of the two locations.",
